# Upstream set `* text eol=lf` and then listed a handful of binary types. Every
# binary type added since has to be listed too, or git will "helpfully" convert
# its line endings and hand back a different file. This one did exactly that to
# two 5.7MB font files: the stored blob came back 94 bytes shorter than the file
# on disk, and a subsetted OpenType table with 94 bytes missing is a font that
# does not load. `git diff` said nothing, because git thought they were text.
#
# The rule: any extension that is not source is binary. Adding an asset type
# here is part of adding the asset.
* text eol=lf

# images
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.car binary
*.svg text eol=lf

# fonts
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.ttc binary

# audio
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.m4a binary

# archives and installers
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.7z binary
*.dmg binary
*.exe binary
*.msi binary
*.deb binary
*.rpm binary
*.snap binary
*.AppImage binary

# misc
*.pdf binary
*.wasm binary
*.node binary
*.sqlite binary
